From 744af6e2c76c177a3e261ff2749a684eb8cadfe8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JimmyBlunt <jo@paso-music.de>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 03:03:26 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] Ausgabe Rand: scaled/rotated patterns fill the whole
 output surface (local #9002)

New per-Pattern Ausgabe setting "Rand" (edge mode, settings field
outputEdge, default 'auto') decides what appears where Scale/Rotate sample
beyond the surface:

- Pixelblaze: frei (default; the transformed coordinates reach the Pattern
  unchanged, like a TouchDesigner shader's UV, so procedural Patterns just
  continue), spiegeln, wiederholen, strecken. The folding modes fold each
  transformed map axis into the active map bounds.
- FastLED surface projection: spiegeln (default; the sketch raster is
  finite), wiederholen, strecken, schwarz (the old black outside). The
  fitted sketch-space position is folded into the sketch raster (padded by
  half an LED) before the nearest-LED lookup, so every unmasked map pixel
  still carries exactly one sketch LED's L2/L1 bytes; masked pixels stay
  black. Rotated corners use the same mode.

Fold math (foldEdge): inside values unchanged; mirror period 2W, wrap
period W, clamp to the edge. Neutral Scale/Rotate never folds (bit-identical
frames, FastLED tables unchanged). Persisted like the other Ausgabe fields
(PatternRecord.settings / demoOverrides); Zuruecksetzen restores the
language default; Rand alone is not "Ausgabe veraendert". Greyed out for the
FastLED index projection. DeckSelect gains disabled/title.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
