e the first frame of a newly opened Pattern, `startLoop` calls `ensureOutputSettingsSeeded()` (the open-time seed effect runs after the build effect); a demo's router frames are held back until `demoOverridesLoaded` so a persisted Helligkeit cannot flash at 100 %. "Zurücksetzen" drops the five fields from the layer-1 bag (`clearPatternSettingsFields` / `clearDemoSettingsFields`). Nothing of this is in pushed code (Send to Controller bundles the source; its JPEG thumbnail renders separately); Shows and static Gallery thumbnails ignore it.
+- Ausgabe (`src/engine/outputAdjust.ts`, deck section "Ausgabe" in `OutputPanel.tsx`, all Patterns, not only FastLED): five per-Pattern controls that reach the router. Settings fields (per-pattern cascaded, `settings.ts`): `outputBrightness` 0..1, `speed` 0..4 (the existing field; the Preview section's speed dropdown is gone, a stored value above 4 clamps to 4 on seed), `outputHue` −180..180°, `outputScale` 0.25..4, `outputRotate` −180..180°, `outputEdge` (Rand: `auto` | `free` | `mirror` | `wrap` | `clamp` | `black`, default `auto` = Pixelblaze `free`, FastLED `mirror`; `effectiveOutputEdge` maps a mode the language does not offer: Pixelblaze `black` → `free`, FastLED `free` → `black`; an unknown stored value reads as `auto`). Layer 1 lives where every other preview override lives: `PatternRecord.settings` (`settings_json`, no migration) for a personal Pattern, `demoOverrides` for a read-only demo / FastLED example; forks copy them like the rest. Chain: Speed scales the frame delta (`renderLoop` `getSpeed`: Pixelblaze `delta`/`time()` and the FastLED virtual clock, i.e. `frame(dt)` to the worker; 0 = frozen), Scale/Rotate move the map coordinates before the Pattern's own transform stack (`createRenderLoop({ getOutput })` → `transformMapCoordinates`: `c + R(−θ)·(p − c)/scale` about the bounding-box centre of the active samples, so the image turns by +θ from +x towards +y; 1D maps zoom x only and have no rotation; 3D maps rotate in the plane of the two largest extents, the plane `largestExtentAxes` gives the FastLED surface projection; for FastLED the loop leaves coordinates alone (`coordinateOutput: false`) and the surface table applies `zoom`/`rotateDeg` to the map positions before flips and fit, swapped live via the handle's `setProjection`; the index projection has no geometry, so the deck greys Scale/Rotate/Rand out). Rand (`foldEdge(x, lo, hi, edge)`: values inside [lo, hi] unchanged; `mirror` reflects with period 2W, `wrap` tiles with period W, `clamp` holds the edge; zero width → lo) applies only off neutral geometry: Pixelblaze folds each transformed map axis (< map dims) into the active samples' bounding box (`MapFrame.min/max`, the normalised space the Pattern sees; `free` = no fold, the TouchDesigner-like pass-through); FastLED folds the fitted sketch-space position (after zoom/rotate, flips and fit) into the sketch bounding box padded by half an LED, then takes the nearest sketch LED as before, so every unmasked map pixel still carries exactly one sketch LED's L2/L1 bytes and masked pixels stay −1; `black` keeps positions outside (→ −1). The table cache key includes the edge mode, then on the finished frame Hue (HSV rotation, keeps max/min channel) → Helligkeit (multiply) → masked pixels stay black → renderer (times the preview-only monitor `brightness`) and `externalPixelOutput`. At neutral values (1, 1, 0°, 1, 0°) nothing is computed and frames are bit-identical (Pixelblaze Fast/Precise, FastLED L1/L2 goldens). The preview-only `brightness` (sun slider) stays a monitor control; it never reaches the router. Before the first frame of a newly opened Pattern, `startLoop` calls `ensureOutputSettingsSeeded()` (the open-time seed effect runs after the build effect); a demo's router frames are held back until `demoOverridesLoaded` so a persisted Helligkeit cannot flash at 100 %. "Zurücksetzen" drops the six fields (incl. `outputEdge`, back to `auto`) from the layer-1 bag; the badge ignores Rand, the reset button is enabled by any Ausgabe override (`clearPatternSettingsFields` / `clearDemoSettingsFields`). Nothing of this is in pushed code (Send to Controller bundles the source; its JPEG thumbnail renders separately); Shows and static Gallery thumbnails ignore it.
 - Preview start: the deck pauses itself while no Pattern is loaded (upstream #478); it now resumes when the pause was automatic and a Pattern arrives (cold load, deep link), while a user pause stays.
 - Controls: FastLED UI elements map to ranged slider/toggle Controls (`PatternMetadata.controls[].range`); values persist in `PatternRecord.controls` (`controls_json`) keyed by UI name.
 - Worker and watchdog: the worker runs the same host calls in the same order, so bytes are identical; frames are pipelined by one IDE frame (frame(dt_k) requests frame k while frame k-1 is shown; a late answer repeats the last frame and the deltas accumulate). No answer within 2 s (setup 10 s) terminates the worker: runtime error, last frame kept. The host's loop/show budget still reports runaway loops that call `millis/delay/show` (they keep running). Measured at 4,593 LEDs: ~1 ms per frame in the worker, ~1.4 ms round trip, main-thread cost ~0.1 ms per frame; added latency one IDE frame.
